>enter into debug (not discover/explore) mode?  You know, the mode where you
>get all those nifty commands like ^W and ^F....

"nethack -D" with a character name of "Wizard" or "wizard" (only 1 works,
I can't remember which) worked for 3.1.1; it shouldn't have changed.

>Second, what is the order of alignment?  I don't really know the difference
>between devoutly, piously, fervently, etc.  What is the list from best to
>worst (or vice-versa)?

I looked in the code for this (since you made me curious)
so I suppose a spoiler doohicky type thing should be used...


Best to worse, worded as shown by a potion of enlightenment or when dead:

"piously aligned"
"devoutly aligned"
"fervently aligned"
"stridently aligned"
"aligned"
"haltingly aligned"
"nominally aligned"
"strayed"
"sinned"
"transgressed"

If you apply a stethescope or zap a wand of probing,
The last three will show as "insufficiently", and 
"aligned" will read as chaotic/neutral/lawful.

